A one-pair example can show a striking local color change, but does not by itself prove a broad rule such as filling an enclosure, propagating color across an object, or encoding every matching marker. Record the exact changed cells and equally important unchanged candidates before generalizing. Keep separate hypotheses for task class, selector, operation, and output representation; avoid collapsing all four into one intuitive visual story.

After a candidate fails, the failure rejects the entire candidate transformation. Reopen those four components rather than making a cosmetic adjustment. A retry should explain all observed edits and non-edits and, when more than one rule remains plausible, use a demo request only for a concrete distinguishing prediction.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen/play/users/u059/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-ledger/references/single-demo-overreach.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-stream-demo-discipline", "file": "references/failed-hypothesis-reset.md", "content": "# Resetting after failed ARC hypotheses

Repeated incorrect outputs indicate the task class or answer representation may be wrong, not merely a coordinate detail. Before spending another attempt, revisit all demonstrations: list input/output dimensions, identify separators and partitions, enumerate each region's candidate features, and test a compact region-summary mapping across every pair. Do not submit a revised pattern unless it exactly reproduces all known demonstrations. A new demo request should target a clearly stated unresolved distinction; serial requests without analysis impose cost without improving inference.

For small outputs from large partitioned canvases, prioritize understanding the relationship between each cell/region and the compact answer. Keep a candidate mapping table and explicitly account for exceptions (e.g. output cells retaining a background/category color). Only after the mapping reproduces all demos should it be applied to the test.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen/play/users/u059/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-stream-demo-discipline/references/failed-hypothesis-reset.md"}
